                  <provenance type="#m" source="3493"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_295">Lanthony (secunda),
                        Gloucestershire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin and St John the
                        Baptist</orgName><p>Lambeth Palace 425, fols. i, 1--21, and 431, fols. 1,
                        1--7, 16--88, formed one volume, earlier at Llanthony Prima, q.v., belonging
                        to a prior. Contents list by Morgan of Carmarthen on fol. 87v.</p><p>London,
                        BL, Royal 2 C.x; Lambeth Palace 30; 80, fols. 168--244; 101; 138, fols.
                        1--44; 148; 153, fols. 156--179; 165, fols. 102--190; 195; 200, fols.
                        114--163; 208; 215; 218, fols. 1--89; 227; 231; 345, fols. 97--227; 360,
                        fols. 1--118; 365, fols. 1--119; 377; 378, fols. i, ii, 1--56, 125--165;
                        390; 394; 397; 398; 409; 449; 452; 481; Oxford, Bodl. Bodley 839, Hatton 49,
                        Corpus Christi Coll. 33, 43; Trinity Coll. 39 have a note of contents in the
                        hand of 'Morganus canonicus de Kermerden' (s. xv), who has written his name
                        in many of the books.</p><p> </p></provenance>
               <provenance type="#i" source="3733"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_327">Llanthony (prima),
                        Monmouthshire. Augustinian priory of St John the Baptist; cell of Lanthony
                        (secunda) from AD 1481</orgName><p>"Iste liber est fratris Walteri de Haya
                        prioris lantonie prime." (s. xiii, fol. i verso).</p><p>Marginalia etc. show
                        that Lambeth Palace 425, fols. 1--21, and 431, fols. i, 1--7, 16--88 formed
                        one volume.</p></provenance>
               </history>
